# water_swamp.fmat — tannin-stained, still, silty water: the bed is gone a
# hand's depth down, the colour is tea-brown, there is no caustic to speak of.
#
# Phase W3's colour fixes: the body is a visible tea-brown rather than near
# black (which left the sky's reflection to colour it all), the reflection is
# tinted olive and rougher, so a marsh pool under a blue sky reads
# green-brown, not cartoon blue.
kind: surface
texture: water
doc: 'Swamp or bog water: tea-brown and opaque, still, dull reflections.'
effects:
  - effect: water
    absorption: 2.4
    shallow_color: {r: 0.56, g: 0.46, b: 0.26}
    scatter_color: {r: 0.13, g: 0.11, b: 0.05}
    subsurface: 0.1
    roughness: 0.18
    refraction: 0.12
    foam: 0.1
    caustics: 0
    flow_speed: 0.03
    wave_amplitude: 0.01
    detail_strength: 0.4
    reflectivity: 0.3
    reflect_color: {r: 0.95, g: 0.9, b: 0.6}
